ates and kingdoms under the umbrella of the Mughals. Falconry, the sport of hunting small game with a bird of prey, was a popular activity among the highest ranks of Mughal royalty. The falcon depicted in this painting appears to be a peregrine. Cords with bells keep the trained hunting bird tethered to its roost.","external_resources":{"wikidata":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60470111"],"internet_archive":["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1968.42-falcon"]},"citations":[],"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1968.42","images":{"annotation":null,"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_web.jpg","width":"579","height":"893","filesize":"109731","filename":"1968.42_web.jpg"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_print.jpg","width":"2205","height":"3400","filesize":"1604205","filename":"1968.42_print.jpg"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_full.tif","width":"5145","height":"7931","filesize":"122441556","filename":"1968.42_full.tif"}},"alternate_images":[{"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_alt0_web.jpg","width":"585","height":"893","filesize":"439029"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_alt0_print.jpg","width":"2226","height":"3400","filesize":"5223166"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_alt0_full.tif","width":"3273","height":"5000","filesize":"49115236"},"date_created":"2005-01-13T16:11:35","annotation":""},{"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_alt1_web.jpg","width":"585","height":"893","filesize":"432487"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_alt1_print.jpg","width":"2226","height":"3400","filesize":"5044467"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1968.42/1968.42_alt1_full.tif","width":"3273","height":"5000","filesize":"49115180"},"annotation":""}],"creditline":"Edward L